The yoagent retry door now honours the retry_after_partial opt-in. It's committed as 9991cb4e, and everything passed: build, the full test suite (6423 passed, 0 failed), clippy with -D warnings, fmt, and tests/harness_logic.sh.

The change: handle_provider_retry in src/prompt.rs used to pass a hard-coded false, so it ignored the opt-in. It now reads it through the same is_retry_after_partial() call the other four retry sites use, with no new config reader. With the opt-in off (the default) nothing changes. The #989 tests that pin that behaviour are unedited and still green.

Measured with the opt-in on, using the same fixtures as the #989 tests. A rate_limit_error mid-stream and a truncated stream are both errors yoagent 0.24.2 retries itself, since its is_retryable covers rate limits and network errors.

| Case | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| Partial text, then a yoagent retry, then success (both fixtures) | stdout "PARTIAL_\n", exit nonzero, 1 request (same as off) | stdout "PARTIAL_\n\nPONG\n", exit 0, 2 requests |
| Dies before any text | PONG\n, 2 requests | unchanged |
| Every attempt dies | — | 24 requests (4 yoagent attempts × 6 yoyo attempts), ~70s, exit nonzero, "failed after 6 attempts" |

On the separator: I measured it rather than assuming it. The existing output code already closes the dying line and opens the retried answer with a newline, so a pipe reader sees the two attempts apart, never glued into PARTIAL_PONG. I didn't add any extra separator. All four new tests compare the full stdout with assert_eq!.

Positive control: putting false back (marked NEUTERED) made both opt_in_provider_retry_after_* tests fail by name, and restoring it made them pass. I ran it twice, the second time because the first run's output was cut off. The tree is clean afterwards.

Docs:
• The old "this door deliberately ignores the opt-in because of #991" sentence in retry_after_partial.rs is now marked superseded, with the reason: #991 hasn't landed, and the upgrade moves Overloaded onto this door.
• `ARCHITECTURE.md` has the before/after readings.
• `docs/src/usage/piped-mode.md` no longer says retries inside the provider library are unaffected, and it now states the worst-case cost.

Two caveats:
• The every-attempt-dies test takes about 70s, which slows down the test suite.
• The commit says "Part of #997", not "Fixes". #997 should stay open until a live Overloaded run on the upgraded yoagent confirms the fix.
